            "review_title": "Review at 342 Lagoon",
            "review_text": "Iratdog\nKerhonkson, New York1265 contributions\n0\nSkin tax. Beware!\nDec 2022 • Solo\nI’m embarrassed to admit I didn’t ask for a price for the twin lobster. Wow! Brazen overreach when I finally got the bill. Can you imagine one million one hundred thousand? That’s 49 dollars USD. As soon as they hit me with this number I knew I was screwed. I messed up, I trusted them. Once you eat it and you didn’t get a price up front it’s their game. \n\nIt’s just another hole in the wall cook stall. They didn’t even have the lobsters. I saw them come in in a bag. I was the only person there. There must have been ten more stalls to pick from right there. Yeah it was ok but the bad taste of being made a fool of made the whole event disappointing.\nRead more\nWritten December 27, 2022\nTuyet\nIm sorry to hear about this. As we also replied to your other review, this is daily prices for fresh sea lobster. This is not a farmed one. You can go to any restaurant in Vung tau and they will have around that price. If you don’t know about the local prices I advise you to use google translate the next time and ask about the price. \n\nAbout getting the lobster from across the street. Yes, that’s our local supplier. We like to buy local and have fresh seafood. We take pride in providing local and delicious seafood. We’ve done so for 16 years and we are highly trusted by the locals in Vung tau.\nRead more\nWritten January 15, 2023\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
